            {
              "id": "53cbda7e-f97e-3c07-bb47-c4d579251344",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions. The destination and source are both pointers, and dataflow analysis suggests that they may refer to overlapping memory. The function used for copying does not guarantee correct behavior when the source and destination overlap, which can lead to unpredictable results or memory corruption. Additionally, there is no evidence of a guard to prevent null pointers for the source, increasing the risk of a crash or further undefined behavior. The destination is not likely to be null, but the source may be. These factors, combined with the high-confidence classification and verdict, indicate a real and actionable issue.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory regions that may overlap, use a memory copy function that is safe for overlapping regions. In C/C++, `memmove` is designed for this purpose, while `memcpy` is not. If `main_stream->memcpy` is a wrapper for `memcpy`, ensure it uses `memmove` instead, or add logic to detect and handle overlap.\n\nFor example, if you control the implementation of `main_stream->memcpy`, update it to use `memmove`:\n\n```cpp\n// Replace the underlying memcpy with memmove to handle overlap safely\nmemmove(src1_ddc, src0_ddc, ggml_nbytes(src0));\n```\n\nIf you cannot change the implementation, add a check before the call to ensure the regions do not overlap, or use a safe copy function directly.\n\nAdditionally, ensure that the source pointer is not null before performing the copy to avoid crashes:\n\n```cpp\nif (src0_ddc != nullptr) {\n    memmove(src1_ddc, src0_ddc, ggml_nbytes(src0));\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
